s not limited to the public sector but also extends its scope to private companies operating within the EU. It encourages the adoption of interoperability principles and standards by private enterprises, enabling them to seamlessly collaborate and integrate their digital systems with those of other organizations. This promotes cross-sectoral cooperation and innovation, leading to the development of new digital products, services, and business models.&#xA;&#xA;To support the implementation of the DBC, the EU provides various tools and resources. These include technical guidelines, reference architectures, best practices, and interoperability frameworks that assist member states and private companies in adopting and implementing interoperability solutions. The EU also facilitates knowledge sharing and collaboration through workshops, conferences, and communities of practice.&#xA;&#xA;In summary, the Digital Exchange Digital Business Capability is a comprehensive framework that aims to enhance IT interoperability among member states and private companies within the EU. It promotes the use of common technical specifications, standards, and protocols, facilitates data sharing and accessibility, ensures trust and security, and encourages collaboration and innovation in the digital economy. By fostering interoperability, the DBC enables the seamless exchange of data, information, and services, driving the digital transformation and integration of the European IT landscape."/>
