y also keep up-to-date with changes in legislation that may affect the organization.&#xA;&#xA;In terms of qualifications, a Public Policy Officer typically holds a bachelor's degree in public policy, political science, law, or a related field. Some positions may require a master's degree or significant work experience in a related field. Key skills for this role include strong research and analytical skills, excellent communication skills, a good understanding of the policy-making process, and the ability to work effectively with a wide range of stakeholders."/>
