    <element xsi:type="archimate:Representation" name="NQads" id="id-8020cf6606f9411abd318068b0334e94">
      <documentation>Description: NQuads is a serialization format used for representing RDF (Resource Description Framework) data that extends the capabilities of the N-Triples format. NQuads provides a straightforward and flexible way to express RDF data in a quad format, which includes an additional context or named graph component. This makes it suitable for representing RDF datasets that involve multiple named graphs or contexts.

Publisher: W3C

Source: https://www.w3.org/TR/n-quads/

LOST view: SV-Functional Architecture Principles

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/NQadsRepresentation

EIRA traceability: eira:DataRepresentation

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-08-20

dct:identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/NQadsRepresentation

</documentation>
