    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Intel IONOS Orbiter Connector" id="id-1e8dfb0a661c4d8ca109b01e75e9a765">
      <documentation>Description: The Intel IONOS Orbiter Connector is an implementation of the Eclipse Dataspace Connector (EDC) specification. It is designed to be interoperable with other EDC-compliant connectors, allowing for the secure and federated sharing of data across different data spaces.

Additional information: It is based on the Eclipse Dataspace Connector (EDC) specification, which is an open standard for connecting data spaces. It is designed to be interoperable with other EDC-compliant connectors, allowing for the secure and federated sharing of data across different data spaces.It is implemented in Java and can be deployed on a variety of platforms, including on-premises servers, cloud platforms, and edge devices. It is available as a free and open source software project. The Intel IONOS Orbiter Connector is a valuable tool for organizations that need to share data securely and efficiently across different data spaces. It is easy to use and deploy, and it is compatible with a wide range of platforms.

Example: The Intel IONOS Orbiter Connector could be used to connect a data space for automotive data with a data space for energy data. This would allow for the sharing of data about vehicle emissions and energy consumption, which could be used to improve the efficiency of transportation systems.

Publisher: Intel

Source: https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/homepage.html

LOST view: TVA-Data Space Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/IntelIONOSOrbiterConnectorApplicationService

EIRA traceability: eira:DigitalSolutionApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-07-20

