    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="European Interoperability TestBed" id="id-8dd0e86023f44c09b37b403e52c243b7">
      <documentation>Description: The Interoperability Test Bed is a service offered by the European Commission’s DIGIT to facilitate the conformance testing of IT systems. The Test Bed is itself a software system that can be both downloaded and installed locally, but also reused through a shared online installation operated by DIGIT. It offers an intuitive web user interface that allows administrators to define their project’s overall testing setup as well as users to connect and run tests.

Publisher: DIGIT, Interoperable Europe Initiative

Source: https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/interoperability-test-bed-repository/solution/interoperability-test-bed/about#:~:text=The%20Interoperability%20Test%20Bed%20is%20a%20service%20offered,through%20a%20shared%20online%20installation%20operated%20by%20DIGIT.

LOST view: TVA-Test Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/EuropeanInteroperabilityTestBedApplicationService

EIRA traceability: eira:ConformanceTestingApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2022-01-18

dct:identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ConformanceTestingApplicationService

</documentation>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2024-01-28"/>
      <property key="dct:publisher" value="DIGIT, Interoperable Europe Initiative"/>
      <property key="dct:description" value="The Interoperability Test Bed is a service offered by the European Commission’s DIGIT to facilitate the conformance testing of IT systems. The Test Bed is itself a software system that can be both downloaded and installed locally, but also reused through a shared online installation operated by DIGIT. It offers an intuitive web user interface that allows administrators to define their project’s overall testing setup as well as users to connect and run tests."/>
      <property key="dct:source" value="https://joinup.ec.europa.eu/collection/interoperability-test-bed-repository/solution/interoperability-test-bed"/>
      <property key="skos:note" value="In terms of the testing approach it follows, the Test Bed is typically used to exchange messages with the software systems being tested, supporting both the sending and receiving of messages, validating all steps against the target specification and according to the specific scenario’s expectations. Such scenarios can focus on technical details but can also be defined at business-level, exposing details only when needed to troubleshoot failures. Furthermore, tests can be designed to cover both normal flows but also edge cases and error scenarios that would be otherwise difficult to replicate."/>
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:SolutionBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="https://www.itb.ec.europa.eu/itb/"/>
      <property key="eira:PURI" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/EuropeanInteroperabilityTestBedApplicationService"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="TVA-Test Enablers [Motivation]"/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="TechnicalApplication"/>
      <property key="eira:implementedBy" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/ConformanceTestingApplicationService"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Apache NiFi" id="id-8ed12676e8e840ba905057efd7d22a3f">
      <documentation>Description: Apache NiFi is an open-source data integration and data flow automation tool that provides a visual interface to easily manage and control the movement of data between different systems. It allows users to design, build, and execute data flows, known as data pipelines, using a web-based graphical user interface (GUI). NiFi supports a wide range of data sources, destinations, and processors, enabling efficient data ingestion, transformation, routing, and monitoring.

Additional information: Apache NiFi is designed to handle real-time data streaming and batch processing, making it suitable for use cases such as IoT data collection, log aggregation, data migration, and data transformation. It provides a scalable and reliable platform for managing data flows across various systems, including databases, cloud storage, messaging systems, and more. NiFi's GUI allows users to visually create and modify data pipelines, making it accessible to both technical and non-technical users. It offers features like data provenance, security, data lineage, and extensive monitoring capabilities. NiFi also supports data governance and compliance requirements through features like data encryption, access control, and auditing.

Example: An example application of Apache NiFi is in a data lake architecture. NiFi can be used to ingest data from various sources like sensors, social media feeds, and databases into a centralized data lake. It can then perform data transformations, filtering, and enrichment before storing the processed data in a suitable format for downstream analytics. NiFi's visual interface makes it easy to design and manage complex data flows, ensuring efficient and reliable data movement within the data lake ecosystem.

Publisher: Apache NiFi - Official Website

Source: https://nifi.apache.org/

LOST view: TVA-Data Management Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ApacheNiFiApplicationService

EIRA traceability: eira:DigitalSolutionApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-07-20

dct:identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ApacheNiFiApplicationService

dct:title: Apache NiFi Application Service

</documentation>
