    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Fraunhofer AISEC Trusted Connector" id="id-a679c058b63144959af8966c20733f67">
      <documentation>Description: The “Trusted IoT Connector”, developed by Fraunhofer AISEC allows for a secure usage of the Internet of Things even for critical processes. It ensures that only trustworthy and non-manipulated devices are used for crucial decisions. A secure execution environment, based on containers, enables the pre-processing of data by apps in the “Connector” itself. Through the enforcement of usage control, it is guaranteed that the data is only used for its designated purpose. In this way, new business models can securely be enabled within the Internet of Things.

Additional information: The Trusted Connector can be used to build secure embedded edge devices with or without hardware trust anchors, or as a cloud-based service for hosting demanding data analysis applications. It was designed with typical IIoT security requirements in mind, and offers a variety of features to protect data and ensure its integrity.

Example: The Trusted Connector could be used to secure a factory floor by ensuring that only trusted devices are allowed to connect to the network. It could also be used to protect sensitive data from unauthorized access, or to ensure that data is processed in compliance with regulations such as GDPR.

Publisher: Fraunhofer AISEC

Source: https://www.aisec.fraunhofer.de/content/dam/aisec/Dokumente/Flyer/Flyer_Trusted_IoT_Connector_engl.pdf

LOST view: TVA-Data Space Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/FraunhoferAISECTrustedConnectorApplicationService

EIRA traceability: eira:DigitalSolutionApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-07-20

dct:identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/FraunhoferAISECTrustedConnectorApplicationService

dct:title: Fraunhofer AISEC Trusted Connector Application Service

</documentation>
