    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Knowledge Exchange" id="id-bf79dfec538847d893cbfbee919ce898">
      <documentation>LOST view: TVA-Knowledge Discovery Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/KnowledgeExchangeApplicationService

EIRA traceability: eira:DigitalSolutionApplicationService

ABB name: egovera:KnowledgeExchangeApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2022-18-01

</documentation>
      <property key="eira:PURI" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/KnowledgeExchangeApplicationService"/>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2023-11-20"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/KnowledgeExchangeApplicationService"/>
      <property key="dct:title" value="Knowledge Exchange Application Service"/>
      <property key="dct:type" value="egovera:KnowledgeExchangeApplicationService"/>
      <property key="skos:definition" value="A Knowledge Exchange Digital Service is an online platform that facilitates the sharing of information, expertise, and insights among individuals, organizations, or communities. It often includes features such as forums, document repositories, collaborative workspaces, and social networking capabilities to enhance communication and collaboration."/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSource" value="Techopedia"/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSourceReference" value="https://www.techopedia.com/definition/26558/knowledge-exchange"/>
      <property key="skos:example" value="A university may use a Knowledge Exchange Digital Service to connect researchers across different disciplines, allowing them to share data, research findings, and methodologies, which can lead to interdisciplinary collaborations and advancements in research.&#xA;A digital platform for healthcare professionals where they can exchange clinical case studies, best practices, and the latest research findings to improve patient care and stay updated with medical advancements.&#xA;A government-initiated service that allows policymakers, experts, and stakeholders to discuss and refine policy proposals, share empirical evidence, and access a repository of historical policy documents and their outcomes."/>
      <property key="skos:note" value="The Knowledge Exchange Digital Service is designed to support the dissemination and collaborative use of knowledge across various domains. It can be tailored to specific industries or areas of interest, such as academia, healthcare, technology, or government. The service typically includes mechanisms for content management, user authentication, and access control to ensure that information is shared securely and with the appropriate audience. Advanced services may incorporate artificial intelligence and machine learning to curate and recommend content to users based on their interests and past interactions. The goal of such a service is to foster innovation, improve decision-making, and enable users to learn from each other's experiences and expertise."/>
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="TechnicalApplication"/>
      <property key="skos:broader" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalSolutionApplicationService"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Knowledge Management" id="id-bfaca0664eef441bb82b6c809e4e5ed1">
      <documentation>Definition: A Knowledge Management Application Service is a software application or service that supports the processes of capturing, organizing, storing, retrieving, and sharing knowledge within an organization. It provides functionalities and tools to facilitate knowledge creation, acquisition, categorization, search, collaboration, and dissemination. The Knowledge Management Application Service typically includes features such as knowledge repositories, document management, collaboration platforms, content categorization, search capabilities, expertise location, and best practice sharing. It enables employees or users to access and leverage the organization's knowledge assets effectively, fostering innovation, decision-making, and continuous learning.

Source: International Journal of Computer Science Issues (IJCSI)

Source reference: http://ijcsi.org/papers/IJCSI-8-2-1-179-186.pdf

LOST view: TVA-Knowledge Discovery Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/KnowledgeManagementApplicationService

EIRA traceability: eira:DataManagementApplicationService

ABB name: egovera:KnowledgeManagementApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2022-01-20

</documentation>
