    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="ESPD-EDM" id="id-5c0dadf660ae494cb8d58cc975f50f76">
      <documentation>Description: The European Single Procurement Document (ESPD) is a standardized form used in public procurement processes within the European Union (EU). As a data object, the ESPD represents a structured document that contains essential information about a supplier or contractor. It includes details such as the company's identification, financial standing, technical and professional abilities, and any legal grounds for exclusion. The ESPD serves as a preliminary self-declaration by suppliers, allowing them to demonstrate their eligibility and suitability to participate in public procurement procedures across EU member states.

Publisher: The Publications Office of the European Union

Source: https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/index.html

LOST view: SV-Business Agnostic Data Models

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ESPD-EDMDataObject

EIRA traceability: eira:DataModelDataObject

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-08-20

dct:identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ESPD-EDMDataObject

</documentation>
