  <folder name="Motivation" id="id-0dad48e7ab84448180018f23471397d2" type="motivation">
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Assessment" name="Gaia-X Data Spaces Community" id="id-203d6d148fa94253b22b475bddaef883">
      <property key="eira:PURI" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/Gaia-XDataSpacesCommunityAssessment"/>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2023-11-20"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/Gaia-XDataSpacesCommunityAssessment"/>
      <property key="dct:type" value="egovera:Gaia-XDataSpacesCommunityAssessment"/>
      <property key="dct:title" value="Gaia-X Data Spaces Community Assessment"/>
      <property key="skos:definition" value="The Gaia-X Data Spaces Community is a collaborative initiative that aims to create a secure and trustworthy data infrastructure in Europe. It brings together various stakeholders, including businesses, research institutions, and public entities, to develop and implement standards for data sharing and usage. The community focuses on creating 'data spaces' - secure virtual environments where data can be shared and analyzed while ensuring privacy and compliance with European regulations. These data spaces are designed to foster innovation, enhance competitiveness, and support the digital sovereignty of Europe."/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSource" value="EIRA Team research"/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSourceReference"/>
      <property key="skos:example" value="The Gaia-X Data Spaces Community is a collaborative initiative aimed at creating a secure and trustworthy data infrastructure in Europe. Here are some examples of the community:&#xA;&#xA;1. Automotive Data Space: This community focuses on the automotive industry, working on solutions for secure data exchange between manufacturers, suppliers, and service providers. They might work on projects like connected cars, autonomous driving, and predictive maintenance.&#xA;&#xA;2. Health Data Space: This community works on solutions for secure and efficient data exchange in the healthcare sector. They might work on projects like electronic health records, telemedicine, and personalized medicine.&#xA;&#xA;3. Agriculture Data Space: This community focuses on the agricultural sector, working on solutions for secure data exchange between farmers, suppliers, and researchers. They might work on projects like precision farming, crop yield prediction, and sustainable farming practices.&#xA;&#xA;4. Energy Data Space: This community works on solutions for secure and efficient data exchange in the energy sector. They might work on projects like smart grids, renewable energy forecasting, and energy efficiency.&#xA;&#xA;5. Public Sector Data Space: This community focuses on the public sector, working on solutions for secure data exchange between government agencies, citizens, and businesses. They might work on projects like e-government, open data, and digital public services.&#xA;&#xA;6. Financial Services Data Space: This community works on solutions for secure and efficient data exchange in the financial services sector. They might work on projects like open banking, fraud detection, and risk management.&#xA;&#xA;7. Manufacturing Data Space: This community focuses on the manufacturing sector, working on solutions for secure data exchange between manufacturers, suppliers, and customers. They might work on projects like Industry 4.0, predictive maintenance, and supply chain optimization."/>
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="skos:note" value="The Gaia-X Data Spaces Community is a collaborative initiative that aims to create a secure, trustworthy, and federated data infrastructure in Europe. This community is part of the larger Gaia-X project, which is a European endeavor to establish a competitive, secure, and trustworthy data infrastructure for Europe.&#xA;&#xA;The Gaia-X Data Spaces Community is composed of various stakeholders, including businesses, research institutions, public sector organizations, and other interested parties. These stakeholders work together to define the requirements, standards, and rules for data spaces, which are virtual environments where data can be shared and exchanged in a secure and controlled manner.&#xA;&#xA;The community's main goal is to create a framework for data spaces that ensures data sovereignty and data availability. Data sovereignty refers to the idea that data is subject to the laws and governance structures of the country in which it is located. Data availability, on the other hand, refers to the ability to access and use data when and where it is needed.&#xA;&#xA;The Gaia-X Data Spaces Community is organized into several working groups, each focusing on a specific aspect of data spaces. These working groups include the Data Spaces Architecture and Standards Working Group, the Data Spaces Use Cases and Requirements Working Group, and the Data Spaces Governance and Certification Working Group.&#xA;&#xA;The community also collaborates with other Gaia-X communities and working groups, as well as with external organizations and initiatives. This collaboration is crucial for ensuring that the data spaces framework is compatible with other components of the Gaia-X infrastructure and with the broader data ecosystem.&#xA;&#xA;In summary, the Gaia-X Data Spaces Community is a collaborative initiative that aims to create a secure, trustworthy, and federated data infrastructure in Europe. It brings together various stakeholders to define the requirements, standards, and rules for data spaces, with the goal of ensuring data sovereignty and data availability."/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="N/A"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Assessment" name="Eclipse Dataspace Components" id="id-4b75e1cf8dd5485fa5e2f89a1eb555b7">
      <property key="eira:PURI" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/EclipseDataspaceComponentsAssessment"/>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2023-11-20"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/EclipseDataspaceComponentsAssessment"/>
      <property key="dct:type" value="egovera:EclipseDataspaceComponentsAssessment"/>
      <property key="dct:title" value="Eclipse Dataspace Components Assessment"/>
      <property key="skos:definition" value="Eclipse Dataspace Components (EDC) is an open-source project under the Eclipse Foundation that provides a platform for developing and managing IoT applications. It offers a set of modular components that can be used to collect, process, and distribute data from various devices and sensors. EDC also supports edge computing, allowing data processing to occur closer to the source, reducing latency and bandwidth usage. It is designed to be flexible and scalable, supporting a wide range of IoT use cases across different industries."/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSource" value="EIRA Team research"/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSourceReference"/>
      <property key="skos:example" value="1. Eclipse Dataspace Connector (EDC): EDC is a software framework that enables secure and reliable data exchange between different systems. It provides a set of APIs and services that allow developers to build applications that can connect, interact, and exchange data with other systems in a secure and reliable manner.&#xA;&#xA;2. Eclipse Dataspace Runtime: This is a runtime environment that supports the execution of applications built using the Eclipse Dataspace Connector. It provides a set of services and capabilities that enable the secure and reliable execution of these applications.&#xA;&#xA;3. Eclipse Dataspace SDK: This is a software development kit that provides a set of tools and libraries that developers can use to build applications that use the Eclipse Dataspace Connector. It includes APIs, documentation, sample code, and other resources that make it easier for developers to build these applications.&#xA;&#xA;4. Eclipse Dataspace Management Console: This is a web-based interface that allows administrators to manage and monitor the operation of the Eclipse Dataspace Connector and the applications that use it. It provides capabilities for configuring the connector, monitoring its operation, and troubleshooting any issues that may arise.&#xA;&#xA;5. Eclipse Dataspace Security Services: These are a set of services that provide security capabilities for the Eclipse Dataspace Connector and the applications that use it. They include services for authentication, authorization, encryption, and other security-related functions."/>
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="skos:note" value="Eclipse Dataspace Components (EDC) is an open-source project under the Eclipse Foundation that aims to provide a set of reusable components for building data-centric applications. These components are designed to help developers manage and manipulate data in a more efficient and effective way.&#xA;&#xA;EDC is built on the Eclipse Modeling Framework (EMF), which is a modeling framework and code generation facility for building tools and other applications based on a structured data model. This allows EDC to provide a consistent and unified approach to data management, making it easier for developers to work with data in their applications.&#xA;&#xA;The components provided by EDC cover a wide range of data management tasks. These include components for data access, data transformation, data validation, and data visualization. Each component is designed to be reusable and customizable, allowing developers to tailor them to their specific needs.&#xA;&#xA;Data Access Components are used for reading and writing data from various sources, such as databases, files, and web services. They provide a unified API for data access, abstracting the underlying data source and allowing developers to work with data in a consistent way.&#xA;&#xA;Data Transformation Components are used for converting data from one format to another. They support a wide range of data formats and provide a flexible and powerful transformation engine.&#xA;&#xA;Data Validation Components are used for checking the integrity and consistency of data. They provide a set of validation rules that can be applied to data to ensure it meets certain criteria.&#xA;&#xA;Data Visualization Components are used for presenting data in a visual format. They support a variety of visualization techniques, including charts, graphs, and tables.&#xA;&#xA;In addition to these components, EDC also provides a set of utilities for common data management tasks, such as data filtering, sorting, and paging.&#xA;&#xA;Overall, Eclipse Dataspace Components is a comprehensive solution for data management in application development. It provides a set of powerful and flexible components that can significantly simplify the task of working with data, allowing developers to focus more on the business logic of their applications."/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="N/A"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Assessment" name="Key Structural IoP Enablers" id="id-4f681942c4654537baaa02232c50a883">
      <property key="dct:type" value="eira:KeyStructuralIoPEnablersAssessment"/>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2024-01-28"/>
      <property key="eira:synonym"/>
      <property key="skos:definition" value="Key Structural IoP Enablers ABB is a Grouping enabling information interpretation to share and/or reuse of organizational resources of digital public services"/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSource" value="ISA2-EIF"/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSourceReference" value="https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/eif_en/"/>
