      <property key="skos:example" value="An example of the application of the Business Agnostic Organisational Agreement Catalogue ABB could be a country developing its National Governance Model for IT interoperability. The country would refer to the catalogue to understand the necessary specifications, agreements, and contracts to be established. This could include agreements on data sharing between government departments, contracts with IT service providers to ensure they adhere to the required standards, and specifications for the IT systems to be used. The catalogue would guide the country in ensuring its National Governance Model aligns with the broader European IT interoperability framework."/>
      <property key="skos:note" value="The Business Agnostic Organisational Agreement Catalogue ABB is a critical tool in promoting seamless interoperability, data security, and efficient digital services within a country. It contains the necessary specifications, agreements, and contracts that define the framework and processes for IT interoperability. This includes the roles and responsibilities of different stakeholders, the standards and policies to be followed, and the guidelines for data exchange and sharing. The catalogue is 'business agnostic', meaning it is applicable regardless of the specific business or industry involved. It aligns with the broader European IT interoperability framework, facilitating cross-border data exchange and cooperation."/>
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="OV-Governance Architecture Principles"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="OV-Data Spaces"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="Organisational view"/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="Organisational"/>
      <property key="skos:broader" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TechnicalAgreementContract"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Grouping" name="Storage Infrastructure Enablers" id="id-173da3c093814ef4bfb91aeb433adcad">
      <documentation>Definition: Storage Infrastructure Enablers ABB is a Grouping of a set of tools and digital services that facilitate the efficient and effective storage of data

Source: TECHNOPEDIA

Source reference: https://www.techopedia.com/definition/30476/storage-infrastructure

Example: The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): GARTNER- Distributed File Systems and Objects Storage Reviews and Ratings. https://www.gartner.com/reviews/market/distributed-file-systems-and-object-storage

LOST view: Technical view - Infrastructure

Interoperability saliency: Storage Infrastructure Enablers ABB is salient for technical interoperability because it establishes the mechanism to (i) ensure the correct management of the information across single or multiple infrastructures, and (ii) minimize the effects of data loss in case of unexpected behaviour of public services through data recovery strategies.

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/StorageInfrastructureEnablers

eira:ID: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/StorageInfrastructureEnablers

ABB name: eira:StorageInfrastructureEnablers

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

</documentation>
