      <property key="eira:PURI" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticConformanceSolutionsGrouping"/>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2024-01-28"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticConformanceSolutionsGrouping"/>
      <property key="dct:title" value="Bussiness Agnostic Conformance SolutionsGrouping"/>
      <property key="skos:example" value="Examples of Business Agnostic Conformance Solutions could include compliance management software like LogicGate or Onspring. These platforms provide tools for risk management, compliance, audit management, and more, and can be used by businesses in any industry. Another example could be a digital service that provides a platform for businesses to manage and monitor their GDPR compliance, which would be applicable to any business that handles personal data of EU citizens."/>
      <property key="skos:note" value="These solutions are typically software or digital services that provide tools and features to help businesses manage and monitor their compliance with various regulations. They may include features for risk management, audit trails, reporting, and more. The 'agnostic' aspect refers to the fact that these solutions are not tied to any specific business or industry - they can be used by any type of business that needs to comply with certain regulations. This makes them highly versatile and useful for businesses operating in highly regulated industries, such as finance, healthcare, and more."/>
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:SolutionBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="dct:description" value="Bussiness Agnostic Conformance Solutions ABB is a grouping that refers to actual solutions that facilitate the alignment of business processes, regardless of the industry or sector, with the necessary regulatory and compliance requirements. These solutions are designed to be adaptable and flexible, allowing businesses from different sectors to conform to the same set of standards or regulations."/>
      <property key="dct:publisher" value="EIRA Team Research"/>
      <property key="dct:source"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="TVA-Test Enablers [Motivation]"/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="TechnicalApplication"/>
      <property key="eira:implementedBy" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalSolutionApplicationService"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Grouping" name="Security Requirements Catalogue" id="id-42a7daa9e3e04bc497a2788e33f9ed9b">
      <documentation>Definition: Security Requirements Catalogue ABB is a grouping that covers a range of non-functional IT requirements that are critical for ensuring the security, integrity, and reliability of a system or application. These requirements include confidentiality, integrity, nonrepudiation, accountability, authenticity, auditability, authentication, authorization, legality, compliance, and privacy. Each of these elements plays a crucial role in protecting sensitive information, preventing unauthorized access or modification, ensuring compliance with laws and regulations, and maintaining the trustworthiness and credibility of the system.

Source: EIRA Team Research

Additional information: The Security Requirements Catalogue ABB is a comprehensive collection of IT security requirements that are essential for any system or application that handles sensitive data. These requirements are designed to protect the data from unauthorized access, ensure its accuracy and consistency, provide proof of transactions, track user activities, verify user identities, grant appropriate access levels, comply with legal and regulatory standards, and safeguard privacy. Failure to meet these requirements can result in security breaches, loss of data integrity, legal penalties, and loss of trust among users and stakeholders.

Example: For example, a healthcare application would need to meet the requirements of confidentiality to protect patient data, integrity to ensure the accuracy of medical records, nonrepudiation to provide proof of medical orders, accountability to track user activities, authenticity to verify the genuineness of data, auditability to provide a record of transactions, authentication to verify user identities, authorization to grant appropriate access levels, legality to comply with healthcare regulations, compliance to adhere to data protection standards, and privacy to safeguard patient privacy.

LOST view: Digital Solution Non-Functional Requirements Catalogue view

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/SecurityRequirementsCatalogueGrouping

ABB name: egovera:SecurityRequirementsCatalogueGrouping

