            <documentation>NARRATIVE:
The TVA-Orchestration Enablers [Motivation] view extends Technical view - application and provides a comprehensive framework for leveraging various elements that facilitate business agnostic orchestration. 

The first element is the &quot;Business Agnostic Orchestration Business Service,&quot; which is a Diagram Model-group ABB. This element encapsulates the &quot;Workflow Management&quot; service, a Business Service ABB that provides a digital public service for managing workflows.

The second element is the &quot;Orchestration Enablers,&quot; a Grouping ABB that refers to the components and practices supporting the development and deployment of orchestration applications. This group includes three sub-elements: &quot;Orchestration&quot; as an Application Service ABB, &quot;Orchestration&quot; as an Application Component ABB, and &quot;Workflow Management&quot; as an Application Service ABB. The &quot;Orchestration&quot; Application Service ABB enables the definition of the sequence and conditions in which one service invokes other services to realize some useful function. The &quot;Orchestration&quot; Application Component ABB enables the coordination and management of the execution of multiple components or services within an application or system. The &quot;Workflow Management&quot; Application Service ABB, also known as Orchestration Application Service, refers to a software solution or service that enables the design, execution, and coordination of workflows within an organization.

The third element is the &quot;Business Agnostic Orchestration Solutions,&quot; a Grouping SBB that serves as a catalogue for orchestration solutions. This group includes two sub-elements: &quot;Apache Airflow&quot; and &quot;Apache Beam,&quot; both of which are Application Service SBBs. These services represent specific orchestration solutions that can be utilized in the orchestration process.

The motivation behind this view is to provide a comprehensive understanding of the various elements and their interrelations that enable effective orchestration in a business-agnostic manner. This includes the services, components, and specific solutions that can be leveraged to design, execute, and manage workflows and orchestration processes within an organization.
</documentation>
          </element>
