            <documentation>Narrative: &#xD;
The &quot;Semantic view - Forms Structure&quot; extends semantic view and provides a comprehensive framework for designing and managing the structure of forms within the digital ecosystem. This view associates the Forms Structure with the Business Information Base and Digital Public Services from the application layer.&#xD;
Within this view, the Forms Structure defines the organization, layout, and components of digital forms used for data collection and input. It ensures a consistent and standardized approach to form design, enhancing user experience, and enabling efficient data capture.&#xD;
The Business Information Base, as part of the application layer, relies on the Forms Structure to ensure effective data collection and management. It utilizes the defined forms structure to design and implement forms that capture domain-specific data accurately and comprehensively.&#xD;
Digital Public Services leverage the Forms Structure to ensure consistent form design and data collection across different services. These services align their data models, operations, and interactions with the defined forms structure, enhancing user engagement and facilitating accurate data entry within the digital ecosystem.&#xD;
By associating the Forms Structure with the Business Information Base and Digital Public Services, the &quot;Semantic view - Forms Structure&quot; promotes standardized form design and enables efficient data capture and management. This view ensures consistency in form layout and components, improves data quality, and enhances user satisfaction within the context of digital public services.&#xD;
The defined forms structure allows for streamlined data collection, reducing errors, and ensuring data completeness. It provides a user-friendly interface for capturing data, guiding users through the necessary fields and data entry requirements.&#xD;
</documentation>
          </element>
