            <documentation>The view that relates Architecture principles to infrastructure layer view functional components is crucial in solutions architecture. This view focuses on how architecture principles influence the design and implementation of functional components within the technical layer. &#xD;
&#xD;
By aligning architecture principles with technical layer view functional components, solutions architects ensure consistency, enhance performance and scalability, promote reusability and maintainability, and support regulatory compliance. This alignment leads to the creation of robust and efficient applications within the technology layer, enabling seamless integration, optimal user experience, reduced maintenance effort, and adherence to legal and industry standards.&#xD;
&#xD;
In summary, aligning Architecture principles with technical layer view functional components ensures consistency, enhances performance and scalability, promotes reusability and maintainability, and supports regulatory compliance. By following these principles, solutions architects can design robust and efficient applications within the technical layer.&#xD;
</documentation>
          </element>
